// t_472ff302, the second hang shape: an unknown type in a LOCAL declaration.
// Before the fix this hung exactly like the parameter form.
//
// Its DIAGNOSTICS are still poor and that is recorded rather than hidden: the
// parser takes 'bogusType x;' as an expression statement, reports a missing
// semicolon, and a later cascade line names the wrong identifier entirely.
// Five errors for one mistake.  This fixture asserts only that the compiler
// TERMINATES and REFUSES - the message quality is its own row, because
// teaching statement parsing to recognise 'identifier identifier ;' as a
// declaration attempt is a real parser change and does not belong in a fix
// whose whole point is that it cannot break anything.
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    bogusType x;
    o = c;
}
